# Secrets for the clean watchers, sourced by watch-movie.sh / watch-tv.sh.
#
# Copy to .env in this directory (gitignored) and fill in. Do NOT put secrets in
# the .plist files here: those are tracked in git.
#
# launchd does not read login shell profiles, so exporting these in ~/.zprofile
# works for an interactive run and is invisible to the watchers under launchd.
#
# TMDB v3 API key. Enables --lookup, which resolves a year for releases whose
# filename has none ("The.End.of.Oak.Street.2160p...mkv"). Without it those
# files are reported as "SKIP (unparsed media)" and never filed.
TMDB_API_KEY=

# Plex token. OPTIONAL. The post-run rescan reads the token Plex itself stores
# on this machine, so normally there is nothing to set here: after a commit run
# CleanMedia asks Plex to scan just the directories it touched, instead of
# waiting for Plex to notice. Plex's own auto-update is unreliable on an
# external volume, which is why renames sometimes appeared at once and
# sometimes not until the hourly scheduled scan.
#
# Set this ONLY to override that, for instance if Plex runs on another host
# (set PLEX_BASE_URL too) or you want a scoped token. An explicit value here
# always wins and Plex's preferences are then never read.
# PLEX_TOKEN=
# PLEX_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:32400
